00:05:21,176 --> 00:05:27,176
Those who survive the ghost ship are better off dead!

2
00:10:42,352 --> 00:10:48,352
Death Ship is a horror, mystery, thriller film directed by Alvin Rakoff.

3
00:16:03,529 --> 00:16:09,529
Survivors of a tragic shipping collision are rescued by a
mysterious black ship which appears out of the fog.

4
00:21:24,705 --> 00:21:30,705
Little do they realise that the ship is actually a Nazi torture ship which has sailed the seas
for years, luring unsuspecting sailors aboard and killing them off one by one.

5
00:26:45,882 --> 00:26:51,882
Captain Ashland, played by George Kennedy.

6
00:32:07,058 --> 00:32:13,058
Trevor Marshall, played by Richard Crenna.

7
00:37:28,235 --> 00:37:34,235
Nick, played by Nick Mancuso.

8
00:42:49,411 --> 00:42:55,411
Margaret Marshall, played by Sally Ann Howes.

9
00:48:10,588 --> 00:48:16,588
Sylvia, played by Kate Reid.

10
00:53:31,764 --> 00:53:37,764
Lori, played by Victoria Burgoyne.

11
00:58:52,941 --> 00:58:58,941
Death Ship is a 1980 horror film directed by Alvin Rakoff and starring Richard Crenna, George Kennedy, Nick
Mancuso, Sally Ann Howes, Kate Reid, Victoria Burgoyne, and Saul Rubinek in an early role.

12
01:04:14,117 --> 01:04:20,117
The screenplay by John Robins was based on a story by Jack Hill and David P.

13
01:09:35,294 --> 01:09:41,294
A British-Canadian co-production, the film was shot on-location in Dauphin
Island, Alabama; Quebec City, Quebec; and the Gulf of Mexico.

14
01:14:56,470 --> 01:15:02,470
It was director Rakoff's only horror film, and upon release received
mixed-to-negative reviews, but is considered a cult classic.

15
01:20:17,647 --> 01:20:23,647
The film explores themes of rescue, ship, nazi, ocean, shipwreck.

16
01:25:38,823 --> 01:25:44,823
The tone is intense and dark and mind_bending.
